/**
 * Owner-authorized synthetic credential-vault probe for Windows.
 *
 * This exercises the real pinned `@napi-rs/keyring@2.1.2` binding, the real
 * `CredentialStore`, and the real optional `CloudAuthController` against one
 * exact synthetic entry. Credentials are generated by the parent in memory as
 * 32 random bytes per token and travel only through a fixed private stdin
 * frame. No credential is written to a file, environment variable, argv, or
 * log. No real account, provider, server grant, or SessionPort token is used.
 *
 * Roles are separate processes:
 *   write       writes the synthetic ready credential through CredentialStore,
 *               verifies exact readback/fingerprint, and exits without delete.
 *   fault       wraps the real scoped vault read with one deterministic
 *               `VaultError("unavailable")`; exercises the real CredentialStore
 *               and controller with no HTTP, write, delete, or retry. This is
 *               fault injection on real composition, not an OS lock test.
 *   read-logout fresh process; verifies the same credential through
 *               CredentialStore, checks real controller status (local read
 *               only), performs local-only logout, checks signed-out and
 *               exact-entry absence, then disposes the owner lease.
 *   cleanup     exact-entry cleanup used only after all earlier children are
 *               verified stopped; re-reads and fingerprint-compares first.
 *
 * The probe never enumerates vault keys or touches a foreign entry. The exact
 * entry is derived from one operator-supplied canonical UUID. A collision stops
 * before mutation. Failure/uncertain states retain the derived entry for manual
 * review rather than blind deletion.
 */
